cters in literature came into the world. He was one of them. Filled with the twists, pathos and unusual characters that sprang from this novelist's extraordinary imagination, The Mystery of Charles Dickens looks back from the legendary writer's death to recall the key events in his life. In doing so, A. N. Wilson seeks to understand Dickens' creative genius and enduring popularity. Following his life from cradle to grave, it becomes clear that Dickens's fiction drew from his own experiences a fact he acknowledged. Like Oliver Twist, Dickens suffered a wretched childhood, then grew up to become not only a respectable gentleman but an artist of prodigious popularity. Dickens knew firsthand the poverty and pain his characters endured, including the scandal of a failed marriage.","publicationYear":2020,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Dickens, charles, 1812-1870","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-mystery-of-charles-dickens-a-n-wilson"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Authors, biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-mystery-of-charles-dickens-a-n-wilson"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"English Novelists","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-mystery-of-charles-dickens-a-n-wilson"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-mystery-of-charles-dickens-a-n-wilson"}],"displaySummary":"In doing so, A. N. Wilson seeks to understand Dickens' creative genius and enduring popularity. Following his life from cradle to grave, it becomes clear that Dickens's fiction drew from his own experiences a fact he acknowledged. Like Oliver Twist, Dickens suffered a wretched childhood, then grew up to become not only a respectable gentleman but an artist of prodigious popularity. Dickens knew firsthand the poverty and pain his characters endured, including the scan